course: dictionary
lesson: 13471
title: Hygienic: clean and free of germs
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Hygienic means clean and free of germs, so it is unlikely to spread illness. When you meet it in a sentence, look for clues about cleaning and germs. «The kitchen worktops were wiped clean, and the food was kept covered.» Those clues show that the kitchen was hygienic.
explain: Ask what word would fit. «It is not hygienic to cough into your hand and then touch the door handle.» Try your meaning in the sentence: it is not clean, so germs can spread. It makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Hygienic is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a hygienic kitchen, hygienic conditions. Its adverb is hygienically, as in «She washed her hands hygienically.» You can also compare: more hygienic and most hygienic show how clean something is.
fact: Hygienic means clean and free of germs.
fact: «Hygienic» can also mean helping to keep things clean and healthy, like «a hygienic way of storing food».
fact: Hygienic habits, such as washing hands and covering sneezes, stop germs spreading.
fact: Hospitals, kitchens and bathrooms must be hygienic.
fact: Useful phrases: hygienic conditions, a hygienic kitchen, it is not hygienic to…, more hygienic.
exercise: «The chef wore gloves and kept the worktops clean to keep the food hygienic.» What does hygienic mean here? | *Clean and free of germs | Cooked for a long time | Cold and wet | Very large and bright
exercise: «It is not hygienic to cough into your hand and then touch the door.» What does this sentence tell us? | Hands should be warm | Doors are always dirty | Coughing is a fun game | *Germs can spread that way
exercise: «The hygienic kitchen had shiny clean tiles.» Find and copy the word that tells you the kitchen was free of germs. | *hygienic | tiles | shiny | kitchen
test: Which word is the adverb in «She washed her hands ___»? | hygienicly | hygienical | *hygienically
test: Which of these would help stop germs spreading? | Sneezing into the air | Leaving food open on the table all day | Touching the bin and then the food | *Washing your hands before you eat
exam: Which sentence uses hygienic correctly? | The bathroom was dirty and full of germs | *Wash your hands and keep the kitchen hygienic | The hygienic bus was very slow to arrive | I felt hygienic after my dinner
